1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,621
The 1904 Olympic marathon might be the strangest race ever run.

2
00:00:05,121 --> 00:00:10,924
St. Louis. About ninety degrees. Dusty dirt roads, with cars kicking up dust in the runners' faces.

3
00:00:11,174 --> 00:00:13,841
And only two places to get water on the whole course.

4
00:00:14,341 --> 00:00:16,858
Thirty-two men started. Only fourteen finished.

5
00:00:17,358 --> 00:00:23,993
Fred Lorz crossed the line first. But he had quit around mile nine, and ridden in a car for most of the next ten miles.

6
00:00:24,243 --> 00:00:25,821
When people found out, he was banned.

7
00:00:26,071 --> 00:00:29,335
He was later forgiven, and won the Boston Marathon the next year.

8
00:00:29,835 --> 00:00:36,086
The real winner, Thomas Hicks, got strychnine, a rat poison, mixed with brandy from his trainers to keep him going.

9
00:00:36,336 --> 00:00:38,512
He finished hallucinating and barely standing.

10
00:00:38,762 --> 00:00:44,138
His time, about three and a half hours, is still the slowest winning time in Olympic marathon history.

11
00:00:44,638 --> 00:00:49,822
A Cuban mailman ran in street clothes, ate rotten apples, took a nap, and still finished fourth.

12
00:00:50,072 --> 00:00:52,973
One runner was chased a mile off course by wild dogs.

13
00:00:53,223 --> 00:00:55,015
Another nearly died from all that dust.

14
00:00:55,515 --> 00:00:56,945
Follow for more weird history.

